{"seq":13,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-no-tool-search-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T21:58:54.263Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0a5f05aa52a50096163c773cd027fe644f6836c437b1fa03887475c59818bb5e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Moss's notes mention two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers checking in at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that it was fixed. The same note has a follow-up item to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea filed it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 support for firmware testing.\n\nWhat I left out:\n- Moss's 2025-09-14 pipeline digest and 2026-03-23 renewal note both cover Quarrendon but give no ticket numbers.\n- #4409, #4412 and FR-882 appear in Moss's Central notes, but they belong to Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply.\n- Marcus's note is about Quarendon Freightways, which is a different company and not a customer.\n\nI only searched the notes Moss saved as files (team digests). I didn't go through Slack messages."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
